# SABOTAGE: T159 account-level NAME-scope on /operator/accounts DEFEATED
# (ADR-044 Amendment-1 §16.2/§16.4a, RP-J-14 shape). The name-mask predicate
# `Samen.Web.Operator.AccountsLive.name_masked?/3` no longer consults the
# operator's `scope_of/2` membership: the `in_scope?/2` result is OR'd with a
# tautology (`is_binary(tenant_org_id)`, true for every real account), so the
# predicate is ALWAYS false — every account NAME renders ungated by scope, the
# exact pre-Amendment "every org name visible to any operator role" hole this
# ruling closes. Mask-by-omission is defeated; the named RED proof leaks.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/operator_accounts_scope_mask_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: a :none-scope operator sees NEITHER name NOR the tenant_org_id handle
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@
   """
   @spec name_masked?(boolean(), Samen.Fleet.Resolution.scope(), String.t() | nil) :: boolean()
   def name_masked?(scope_masking?, name_scope, tenant_org_id) do
-    scope_masking? and not Samen.Fleet.Resolution.in_scope?(name_scope, tenant_org_id)
+    scope_masking? and not (Samen.Fleet.Resolution.in_scope?(name_scope, tenant_org_id) or is_binary(tenant_org_id))
   end

   # The acting operator id used to read `scope_of/2`: the authenticated principal
